    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** anchoring the lineup, carrying the highest efficiency score of 79.39. His matchup against McGreevy is primed for production, bolstered by an 11% boost from the pitcher\u2019s skill profile and a strong platoon advantage. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** (78.13) and **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) are high-ceiling starts against Smith-Shawver and Chandler, respectively; both benefit significantly from favorable opposing xERAs, providing the secondary power surge necessary to remain competitive in our tight Roto categories. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (74.34) remains an elite cornerstone, seeing his base projection elevated by nearly 20% due to Dobnak\u2019s vulnerable 4.79 xERA.\n\nWhile the core is set, we are monitoring the SB volatility inherent in our roster construction. **Miguel Vargas** (55.28) and **Nasim Nunez** (54.10) were prioritized over bench options specifically because their matchups feature \"Slow SP Delivery\" profiles, increasing their stolen base probability\u2014a crucial needle-mover for our league standings. **Luis Robert Jr.** presents the most significant risk today; his score plummeted to 45.14, largely due to a harsh dynamic platoon penalty and May\u2019s elite ability to hold runners, which effectively handcuffs his primary value as a speed threat. \n\nThe most difficult exclusion was **Heliot Ramos**, who narrowly missed the cut behind the established platoon-favored outfielders. While **Heliot Ramos** remains a potent weapon, his current absence from the confirmed lineup renders him a non-factor for today\u2019s points. We continue to hold **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** on the IL, hoping for imminent returns to bolster our depth. With no extreme weather flags reported, our primary concern is ensuring **Luis Robert Jr.** can overcome his challenging matchup to justify his roster spot, while we look to **Drake Baldwin** to capitalize on his leadoff position against Sasaki to provide an early spark for our Roto totals.",
